# BOX JUMP

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Box Jump is an explosive plyometric exercise designed to develop lower-body power through maximal vertical propulsion followed by a controlled landing on an elevated surface.

Within CAS, it is considered a foundational plyometric exercise for improving explosive power while minimizing landing impact.

---

# Philosophy

The objective of the Box Jump is not to jump onto the highest possible box.

The objective is to produce maximal explosive intent while landing safely.

CAS prioritizes jump quality over box height.

